{"run":{"startedAt":"2026-11-02T13:39:40.522Z","commit":"1db603b73","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5","runtime":"A test build, Chromium's sandbox on, Analyses in Pyodide in the hidden window"},"answers":[{"task":"L06","language":"en","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5","inputs":"893937d3dae364fc092bc1e8240042f7adf19d56d69366a447ede71bb4a77dac","documents":[{"name":"Store takings October.csv","english":"Store takings October.csv","added":true,"status":"ready","problem":null}],"question":"Store takings October.csv is an export from our tills: one row for each takings report a store sent in October, with the takings in yuan. Some amounts were typed with full-width digits, thousands separators or a yuan sign. What is the total takings and how many rows are there? List what you had to normalise to add the amounts up.","answer":{"status":"done","text":"I could not work out the total, but the export has 310 rows. The spreadsheet reader did not keep the text of the 151 amounts it could not read as numbers, so I could not add them up reliably. I did not estimate the total.\n\n**Row count: 310.** The sheet covers A1:C311, which is a header plus 310 data rows[^1]. The last row is store 中关村门店 on 2026-10-31[^2].\n\n**What needs normalising before the amounts can be added:**\n- **Full-width digits**, such as \"２０，６６７．６３\" (朝阳门店, 2026-10-01), which must become ASCII digits[^3].\n- **Yuan signs**, such as \"￥10,181.83\" (国贸门店, 2026-10-03), which must be removed[^4].\n- **Thousands separators**, both ASCII commas like \"10,181.83\" and full-width ones like \"１３，５２６．８７\"[^6]. These must be removed[^4].\n- **Plain decimals with no separators**, such as \"11773.80\", which need no change[^5].\n\nAbout 151 amounts had at least one of these problems. I did not count how many had each one.\n\nTo get the total, export the amount column as plain text, or paste the amounts as text, and I can normalise and add them.\n\n","citations":[{"marker":1,"passageId":"2cacd917-12fd-43c4-87bc-667901